[statement]
Where several conditions name one name, the preliminary choices take their
packages in the order of their names, not the order the repository lists
them. `rb` is listed before `ra`, but `ra`, whose dependency `Y` has `lo`
alone, comes first: `lo` is chosen for `Y` before `X` is reached, and
answers `X`, which `top` states first, so `hi` is not installed. Neither
condition ever holds.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:n w v

P:n
V:1

P:rb
V:1
i:n zz
D:X

P:ra
V:1
i:n zz
D:Y

P:hi
V:1
k:100
p:X

P:lo
V:1
p:X Y=1

P:w
V:1
D:X

P:v
V:1
D:Y

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install n 1
install lo 1
install w 1
install v 1
install top 1
